1. Document Status

This document is a non-canonical design-control file created for generative AI layout assistance, constraint propagation, architectural sketching, geometry auditing, and physical mockup planning.

It does not represent verified, certified, or final engineering designs. It serves strictly as a living sandbox and logical constraint manager to coordinate ideas between founder review, system-architecture review, repository-control review, and editorial organization.

2. Purpose and Authority Boundary

This file governs candidate geometry generation, spatial arrangement, and structural rules. It acts as a safety boundary to prevent hallucinated spatial errors or unsafe structural configurations during AI-assisted design loops.

Canonical subsystem files remain the authoritative sources of truth for subsystem mechanics, materials, chemical workflows, power architecture, validation state, and physical test results. If a structural layout generated using this file conflicts with an authoritative subsystem specification, the subsystem specification always takes precedence.

3. Current Boat Ruling

The core architectural directive of this vessel is preserved as follows:

The boat is a clean, inspectable, ballast-testable support raft, not a processing vessel.

The physical system must be optimized for visual inspectability, rapid leak detection, clear structural access, and clean/dirty separation. It does not carry raw, uncontained sargassum biomass, nor does it host biological digestion systems directly on its main deck structure unless explicitly governed by validated interface and containment logic.

