12. Physical Mockup Package

To validate the geometry before sourcing production-grade materials, physical mockups are required. The following mockups must be built, tested, and documented:

[MOCKUP PLACEHOLDER: DRUM RESTRAINT BAY]

Objective: Build a 1-to-1 scale single-drum bay frame using candidate restraint and strap hardware.

Test Questions / Failure Signs:

Does the drum unit shift, creep, deform, or loosen under candidate force loads?

Is manual drum removal or swapping hindered during operation?

What failure signs are observed under simulated cyclic strain?

What measurement does this mockup unlock?

What parameters remain unresolved?

[MOCKUP PLACEHOLDER: PVC TRUSS BAY]

Objective: Assemble a section of the distributed short-span PVC truss chassis [CANDIDATE FOOTPRINT PLACEHOLDER — PENDING VALIDATION].

Test Questions / Failure Signs:

How does the frame deflect under a distributed candidate payload?

Are there signs of joint cracking, permanent distortion, racking, or fastener shearing?

What measurement does this mockup unlock?

What parameters remain unresolved?

[MOCKUP PLACEHOLDER: REMOVABLE DECK PANEL BAY]

Objective: Fabricate candidate deck panels using light grating materials over the truss mockup.

Test Questions / Failure Signs:

Does the panel lift clear using the single-hand candidate pull loop, or does it bind and resist removal?

Does the panel wobble, rattle, or shift under candidate dynamic live footwork?

Does the panel design block visual inspection of critical underlying joints or restraints?

What measurement does this mockup unlock?

[MOCKUP PLACEHOLDER: REINFORCED SKID BAY]

Objective: Create a mock skid assembly representing heavy equipment and mount it to the truss chassis mockup.

Test Questions / Failure Signs:

Does the sub-deck frame transfer the localized mock equipment load without crushing candidate tubes or bending joint pins?

Are there visible failure signs such as joint creep, rail shifting, or deck panel sag?

Does the skid installation induce twists or concentrated structural warping across the surrounding chassis bays?

What measurement does this mockup unlock?

[MOCKUP PLACEHOLDER: SACRIFICIAL INTERFACE MODULE]

Objective: Build a physical mock hose-and-connector panel at the deck-edge zone.

Test Questions / Failure Signs:

Do the quick-disconnect couplings cleanly decouple when tensioned under candidate force and angle ranges?

Does the coupling pull-action cause structural deformation to the mounting plate or adjacent chassis nodes?

Does the breakaway mechanism fail to activate, causing direct pull strain on upstream mock process components?

Where does residual fluid pool, and what drip containment failure signs are observed?

