15. Jared Editing Rules

To maintain the repository integrity and claim safety of this design file, the Editor (G/Gemini/Jared) must strictly adhere to the following guardrails during all future updates:

Rule 1: Do not promote candidate geometry into final design. Keep all references to footprint, dimensions, and positions clearly marked as "candidate," "mock," or "working."

Rule 2: Do not remove validation states. All draft revisions must display the [NON-CANONICAL DESIGN CONTROL FILE — PENDING VALIDATION] header.

Rule 3: Do not erase unresolved variables. The list in Section 14 must only be modified to update current target estimates or log verification results. Do not delete active structural risks.

Rule 4: Do not convert measurement plans into verified results. Only real-world test telemetry or manual physical measurement inputs may move a variable from "unresolved" to "verified."

Rule 5: Do not make safety claims. Avoid any commercial, seaworthiness, safety, payload, stability, or operational-envelope certifications.

Rule 6: Preserve machine-readable sections. Ensure Section 10 (Geometry Rule Sheet) maintains clean, valid, un-embellished YAML blocks. Do not convert them into long prose.

Rule 7: Use plain technical language. Avoid flowery prose. Keep explanations clear, rigorous, and direct.

Rule 8: Do not use "safe" unless referring to a prohibited claim, safety priority, or future validation objective.

Rule 9: Do not define success criteria without approved thresholds.

Rule 10: Do not introduce candidate force, time, deflection, clearance, scale, or reach values unless placed in a separate candidate-notes area and tagged [CANDIDATE PLACEHOLDER — PENDING VALIDATION].

Rule 11: Do not imply environmental release is acceptable.

Rule 12: Do not imply progression from mockup to fabrication is automatic.

