B. Boundary Priority Classes

Boundary Class

Definition

hard separation candidate

intended to minimize direct interaction between clean-side and dirty-side zones

controlled crossing candidate

intended to permit limited hose/cable/interface interaction through visible candidate paths

sacrificial interface candidate

intended to localize strain, contact, routing, or replacement interaction into replaceable boundary elements

inspection boundary candidate

intended to preserve visibility and post-event observation across the boundary

emergency isolation candidate

intended to preserve reachable shutdown/isolation logic from clean-side access paths

unresolved boundary condition

interaction or crossing logic remains contradictory, undefined, or dependent on future mockups

No class implies validated containment, validated safety, or operational approval.

